{
  "quest.4F5379677AA39981.title": "ForceCraft",
  "quest.4F5379677AA39981.quest_desc": [
    "&2Power Ore&r shows up in stone and deepslate across the Overworld, and Nether Power Ore in netherrack.",
    "",
    "Mine some &aForce Gems&r. Everything else in &eForceCraft&r starts with them.",
    "",
    "Each ore drops 2 to 4 gems, and Fortune adds more. You'll need an iron pickaxe or better to mine it.",
  ],
  "quest.79A6DFDB960DE9BF.title": "Heavy Metal",
  "quest.79A6DFDB960DE9BF.quest_desc": [
    "Most of what you build next needs metal as well as gems.",
    "",
    "Make a few &aForce Ingots&r. You'll go through them quickly.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: JEI shows two ways to make them, and one gives more ingots per gem.",
  ],
  "quest.6EA5EF67B6076C87.title": "Spare the Rod",
  "quest.6EA5EF67B6076C87.quest_desc": [
    "The &aForce Rod&r is this mod's multi-tool, and its first job is starting a tree farm.",
    "",
    "Make a &aForce Rod&r, then Right-click a vanilla sapling with it to turn it into a &2Force Sapling&r.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The first rod you can make starts with only 2 uses left. Spend them on saplings, since a Force Tree is what gets you a rod that lasts.",
  ],
  "quest.4FAD557994987780.title": "Branching Out",
  "quest.4FAD557994987780.quest_desc": [
    "Force Trees grow wild in forests, and you can plant a &2Force Sapling&r anywhere you like.",
    "",
    "Grow a Force Tree and chop some &aForce Logs&r. Plant a few saplings so you aren't waiting on a single tree.",
    "",
    "Force Leaves sometimes drop &2Force Nuggets&r along with saplings.",
  ],
  "quest.2B12C442D45A6DB1.title": "Light the Way",
  "quest.2B12C442D45A6DB1.quest_desc": [
    "Force Torches give off full light, level 15.",
    "",
    "Make a &aGolden Power Source&r and some &2Force Torches&r. Keep a few spare for the special torches later in this chapter.",
    "",
    "They can also be dyed.",
  ],
  "quest.5323AFD2CA835C79.title": "Transmutation",
  "quest.5323AFD2CA835C79.quest_desc": [
    "A &aForce Rod&r can transmute one item into another.",
    "",
    "JEI's Transmutation tab lists everything the rod can convert. Each one costs the rod 1 durability.",
    "",
    "Old iron, gold and diamond gear transmutes back into ingots and diamonds, as long as it's undamaged.",
  ],
  "task.2AE2563B5A919904.title": "Transmutation",
  "quest.17B12D94FEDD135B.title": "&6Force Infuser",
  "quest.17B12D94FEDD135B.quest_subtitle": "Unlocks tool upgrades",
  "quest.17B12D94FEDD135B.quest_desc": [
    "The &aForce Infuser&r adds upgrades to Force tools, armor and torches.",
    "",
    "Place a &aForce Infuser&r and make an &2Upgrade Tome&r for it. Nothing happens without a tome in its slot.",
    "",
    "Every upgrade uses 1,000 mB of &bLiquid Force&r, and the Infuser needs FE to run. Force Gems in the gem slot turn into 250 mB each.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The tome sets how many upgrade slots are open: 2 at Tier 1 and one more each tier, up to all 8 at Tier 7.",
    "",
    "It earns points from every upgrade you apply. The most come from upgrades of the tome's current tier that you haven't used at that tier yet.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The guide button in the Infuser's screen lists the upgrades your tome has reached.",
  ],
  "quest.555AB4E7261A508A.title": "Engine Room",
  "quest.555AB4E7261A508A.quest_desc": [
    "The Infuser uses 20 FE every tick it works. Any FE generator will do, and &eForceCraft&r has one of its own.",
    "",
    "Build a &aForce Engine&r and place it by clicking on the Infuser, so the Engine faces into it. It only runs while it has a redstone signal.",
    "",
    "Force Gems in its fuel slot become Liquid Force worth 20 FE/t, exactly enough for one Infuser. Water in its second tank doubles that, and milk gives 2.5 times as much.",
  ],
  "quest.6F8FEF46F64C860D.title": "Supercharged",
  "quest.6F8FEF46F64C860D.quest_desc": [
    "Once the Infuser has power and Liquid Force, it's ready for its first tool.",
    "",
    "Make a &aForce Pickaxe&r and give it at least one upgrade in the Infuser. Speed is an easy first choice and makes it mine faster.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: A tool can only be infused once, so everything you want on it goes into the same infusion. For a tool you plan to keep, wait until your tome has more slots open.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "An infused tool in the Infuser with every upgrade slot empty gets charged instead. That repairs it and stores Force, which is used up before durability.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"You can also hold the tool and press \", {\"keybind\": \"key.forcecraft.force\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: V\"}}, \" to add \", {\"text\": \"Force Gems\", \"color\": \"green\"}, \" by hand. Each gem stores 250 Force, up to 10,000.\"]",
  ],
  "task.2286A8784C4C0DA2.title": "Infused Force Pickaxe",
  "quest.27368933A8628910.title": "Claws Out",
  "quest.27368933A8628910.quest_desc": [
    "Bats drop &aClaws&r now and then, and the Infuser has a use for them.",
    "",
    "Make a &aForce Sword&r and collect a &2Claw&r.",
    "",
    "The sword takes more kinds of upgrade than anything else in the mod. With Ender, Sneak + Right-click teleports you to the block you're looking at, and Freezing stops whatever you hit from moving or jumping for 5 seconds.",
  ],
  "quest.1A64B4AD3C098087.title": "Take a Bow",
  "quest.1A64B4AD3C098087.quest_desc": [
    "The &aForce Bow&r has five firing modes.",
    "",
    "Make a &aForce Bow&r and a stack of &2Force Arrows&r, the only arrows it fires.",
    "",
    "Sneak + Right-click switches modes. Torch mode fires a torch from your inventory and places it where it hits, and the Ice, Fire and Ender modes need the bow to have Freezing, Heat or Ender.",
  ],
  "quest.69BF9670BBE52AD3.title": "Bringing Home the Bacon",
  "quest.69BF9670BBE52AD3.quest_desc": [
    "Leather, feathers and bacon don't have to cost an animal its life.",
    "",
    "Make &aForce Shears&r and use them on a pig to get &2Raw Bacon&r.",
    "",
    "Cows give leather and chickens give feathers the same way. Each animal turns into a cold version afterward and can't be sheared again.",
  ],
  "quest.738F0A20CF5C4D20.title": "Suit Up",
  "quest.738F0A20CF5C4D20.quest_desc": [
    "Force armor takes upgrades just like the tools.",
    "",
    "Make all four pieces of Force armor, from the &aForce Cap&r down to the &2Force Boots&r.",
    "",
    "Each piece is infused on its own, so you can spread upgrades across the set. Speed adds step height and movement speed, and Camo makes the armor invisible.",
  ],
  "quest.7A86B84D408B6806.title": "Experience Pays",
  "quest.7A86B84D408B6806.quest_desc": [
    "Experience levels are easy to lose on a bad death.",
    "",
    "Make an &aExperience Tome&r. Right-click puts your experience into it, and Sneak + Right-click takes out enough for your next level.",
    "",
    "Keep it topped up, because the next quest uses a lot of it.",
  ],
  "quest.1300778A26F02F29.title": "Core Values",
  "quest.1300778A26F02F29.quest_desc": [
    "The experience in your &2Experience Tome&r can be spent as well as stored.",
    "",
    "Make an &aUpgrade Core&r. JEI's Transmutation tab shows how, and each core costs 100 experience points from the tome.",
  ],
  "quest.77D81B88D6837BDA.title": "Hot Stuff",
  "quest.77D81B88D6837BDA.quest_desc": [
    "Your Upgrade Core needs somewhere to go.",
    "",
    "Build a &aForce Furnace&r. It cooks twice as fast as a vanilla furnace, and the core in its upgrade slot changes what it does.",
    "",
    "It sends finished items into the inventories next to it, except hoppers and other furnaces.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: A core can only be taken back out while sneaking.",
  ],
  "quest.5CFFEEB43351C2C4.title": "Core Curriculum",
  "quest.5CFFEEB43351C2C4.quest_desc": [
    "With an empty upgrade slot, a Force Furnace only smelts.",
    "",
    "Make any one of these five cores and put it in the slot:",
    "",
    "- &aSpeed Core&r: Five times vanilla speed, burning fuel five times as fast too.",
    "",
    "- &aHeat Core&r: Twice the Force Furnace's speed on the same fuel.",
    "",
    "- &aExperience Core&r: Double the experience from smelting.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "- &aGrinding Core&r: Grinds instead of smelting. JEI has a Grinding tab for it.",
    "",
    "- &aFrozen Core&r: Freezes instead of smelting, with its own Freezing tab.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The Frozen Core uses up the bucket when it freezes water or lava.",
  ],
  "task.61606A1940D08110.title": "Any Furnace Core",
  "quest.2051AD25753E9D28.title": "Torch Song",
  "quest.2051AD25753E9D28.quest_desc": [
    "Four special torches each do a job around your base:",
    "",
    "- &aHeat Torch&r: Sets nearby undead on fire.",
    "",
    "- &aHealing Torch&r: Heals nearby players and hurts undead.",
    "",
    "- &aBane Torch&r: Kills every hostile mob within 3 blocks, every 9 seconds.",
    "",
    "- &aCamo Torch&r: Gives off light while staying invisible.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Make any one of them. JEI's Infuser tab shows what each needs, and they take a Tier 4 or Tier 5 tome.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: Keep Bane Torches away from any mob farm you want to keep running.",
  ],
  "task.73A904C3880B4949.title": "Any Special Torch",
  "quest.3E85409498389887.title": "&6Tome Mastery",
  "quest.3E85409498389887.quest_subtitle": "Unlocks all 8 upgrade slots",
  "quest.3E85409498389887.quest_desc": [
    "Every tier of the &aUpgrade Tome&r opens another slot and a new set of upgrades. Tier 7 is the last.",
    "",
    "Bring your tome to Tier 7 and give a &aForce Sword&r Light or Treasure, the two upgrades only Tier 7 offers. Light makes the sword far stronger against undead.",
    "",
    "With all 8 slots open, this is the time to build the tools you plan to keep for good.",
  ],
  "task.3491118B1C03A576.title": "Force Sword with Light or Treasure",
  "quest.307974E72C05EB31.title": "About Time",
  "quest.307974E72C05EB31.quest_desc": [
    "The Time upgrades need one part from outside &eForceCraft&r.",
    "",
    "Make a &aTemporal Core&r. It becomes available once you've finished &6Free the End&r in Generating Resources.",
    "",
    "It unlocks the &2Time Torch&r and the Rod of Time. Sneak + Right-click a Rod of Time to pick Stop, Slow, Fast or Hyper, then Right-click a block to apply that speed to the machines and mobs around it.",
    "",
    "[\"\", {\"text\": \"Go to Free the End\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"id\": \"ftbquests:link\", \"payload\": {\"quest_id\": \"1C742A1E7C1F1059\", \"page\": 1}, \"action\": \"custom\"}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Go to Free the End Quest\"}}]",
  ],
  "quest.2C4167521D4F14EE.title": "&6Time Torch",
  "quest.2C4167521D4F14EE.quest_subtitle": "Speeds up nearby machines",
  "quest.2C4167521D4F14EE.quest_desc": [
    "A &aTime Torch&r speeds up the machines around it for as long as it stays placed, with no fuel or power.",
    "",
    "Make a &aTime Torch&r and Right-click it to cycle through Stop, Slow, Fast and Hyper.",
    "",
    "Fast runs nearby machines at double speed and Hyper at four times. It reaches 3 blocks in every direction, and crops and mobs aren't affected.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: A new Time Torch starts on Stop, which freezes the machines around it. Switch it to Fast or Hyper right after placing it.",
  ],
  "quest.1EDDEC2F46E13705.title": "Small Problem",
  "quest.1EDDEC2F46E13705.quest_desc": [
    "&eForceCraft&r adds Ender Tots and Creeper Tots, small mobs that spawn in the Overworld alongside the usual monsters.",
    "",
    "Defeat an &aEnder Tot&r.",
    "",
    "Creeper Tots are harmless, since their explosion is only fireworks.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: Killing an Ender Tot up close brings 1 or 2 Angry Endermen after you. Arrows don't set them off.",
  ],
}
